cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use LintBench, please cite it as below."
title: "Replication Package for \"How Far Can LLMs Go in Generating Android Lint Checks from Natural Language?\""
type: software
abstract: >-
  Artifact for the paper "How Far Can LLMs Go in Generating Android Lint Checks from
  Natural Language?". LintBench is a 148-instance benchmark (113-instance human-verified subset) for
  evaluating LLMs on generating Android Lint detectors from natural-language issue
  specifications, with a Dockerised Lint test harness. It uses a
  retrieval-augmented, generation and repair pipeline evaluated on the same instances.
